# NetSec - the access points the world is missing.
#
# NetSec gates a network behind its access point. Some networks do not have one
# you can reach, and a mod that locks doors without supplying keys is half a
# mod. These are the keys, placed by hand where the world needed one.
#
# WHY A BLOCK AND NOT A LIST OF SECTORS - the thing that cost weeks.
#
# An earlier attempt declared the sector directly:
#
#     streaming:
#       sectors:
#         - path: netsec_accesspoint.streamingsector
#
# Nothing ever spawned, and ArchiveXL never complained - because nothing was
# malformed. `sectors:` is for EDITING a sector that already exists, which is
# why every entry under it in every other mod carries `expectedNodes` and a list
# of nodeDeletions or nodeMutations against vanilla content. It is not a way to
# introduce one.
#
# A NEW sector has to be registered in a streamingblock, and the block is what
# gets declared. Confirmed against ###_longer_lockdown.archive.xl, a World
# Builder mod installed and working on this machine, which ships
# `<name>\sectors\*.streamingsector` beside `<name>\all.streamingblock` and
# declares only the block. Surveying every .xl in the load order also settled
# the other half: 2,243 expectedNodes, 1,408 nodeDeletions, 1,040 nodeMutations,
# 125 blocks - and ZERO nodeAdditions. There is no way to add a node to a vanilla
# sector, so this is not one route among several. It is the only one.
#
# ON AlwaysLoaded.
#
# Both the sector and its descriptor use category AlwaysLoaded, matching the
# working example rather than the "Exterior" the World Builder export suggests.
# The reasoning: an Exterior sector is found through the world's own streaming
# grid, and nothing registers a mod's block into that grid - so a category that
# depends on it may simply never be reached. AlwaysLoaded does not depend on it.
#
# The cost is real and worth writing down before this list grows: an
# AlwaysLoaded sector is resident. One access point is nothing; several hundred
# is a decision that needs measuring rather than assuming. Revisit before this
# file gets long.
streaming:
  blocks:
    - netsec_access_points\all.streamingblock
